review:
Pro's: 
- The art and story are pretty decent for a Hidden-Objects game; 
- Playtime is about 3-4 hours which is fair for the price on sale;
- Entertaining if you're looking for something easy to play.

Cons: 
- The minigames are too simple;
- The Hidden-Objects games aren't challenging either; 
- Unless you choose to play the hardest mode, the game shows you where too look too fast.

Altogether, I thought the game was a little disappointing because it was too easy, but the game designers made a proper game which was fairly entertaining for any Hidden-Objects/point-and-click fan (though I would recommend if you're interested, you buy it on sale).
